AvatarForcing
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
"Avatar Forcing: Real-Time Interactive Head Avatar Generation for Natural Conversation"
Taekyung Ki, Sangwon Jang, Jaehyeong Jo, Jaehong Yoon, Sung Ju Hwang. CVPR 2026.
Code and checkpoints: https://github.com/TaekyungKi/AvatarForcing (CC BY-NC 4.0)
This port was made against commit 507e3046ad539c938e0412ac7a74cf6e3ba2a61c.

Changes made in this project (CC BY-NC 4.0 §3(a)(1)(B)):

  - src/avatarforcing_mlx/flow_transformer.py, helpers.py — the flow transformer
    (models/avatarforcing/flow_transformer.py) re-implemented in MLX: same module tree,
    parameter names and math; RoPE via mx.fast.rope; KV-cache updates by rebinding
    instead of in-place writes; conditioning modules kept in float32.
  - src/avatarforcing_mlx/sampler.py — the sampling loop (AvatarForcing.sample /
    solve_cfg / solve_closed / prepare_cfg_condition / update_kv_cache) re-implemented
    in MLX; solve_closed's coefficients precomputed in float64 with numpy; the final
    no-op denoising step (t = 0 -> 0) skipped; the user-conditioning CFG branch dropped
    when it has no effect (no user inputs, or u_cfg = 0).
  - src/avatarforcing_mlx/decoder_fast.py — runtime replacements (opt-in, via patch())
    for ModulatedConv2d.forward, upfirdn2d and ToFlow.forward from
    models/avatarforcing/styledecoder.py: algebraically identical rewrites for speed.
  - src/avatarforcing_mlx/preprocess.py — the face-crop logic of inference.py
    (DataProcessor.preprocess_face) and preprocess_user_video.py, on in-memory arrays.
  - src/avatarforcing_mlx/weights.py — converts the published flow_transformer.pth to
    MLX safetensors (key selection, mask buffers dropped, nn.MultiheadAttention's
    packed projections split; values unchanged).
  - src/avatarforcing_mlx/torch_models/ — PyTorch files vendored unmodified except
    for import paths (see the header of each file):
      models/__init__.py -> base.py, models/wav2vec2.py -> wav2vec2.py,
      models/avatarforcing/{encoder,generator,styledecoder}.py -> avatarforcing/,
      the AudioEncoder class of models/avatarforcing/AvatarForcing.py -> audio_encoder.py
  - src/avatarforcing_mlx/configs/inference.yaml — vendored unmodified.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This package does not include or redistribute model weights. `avatarforcing-mlx
download` fetches them from where their authors publish them:

  - flow_transformer.pth, motion_autoencoder.pth — AvatarForcing authors' Google Drive
    (linked from https://github.com/TaekyungKi/AvatarForcing). The flow transformer is
    converted locally to MLX format. The motion autoencoder is derived from FLOAT's
    (below); use it under its authors' terms.
  - facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h — https://huggingface.co/facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h
    (Apache License 2.0), by Facebook AI Research: Baevski, Zhou, Mohamed, Auli,
    "wav2vec 2.0", NeurIPS 2020.

